# Scratch queue rows RING (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/RING.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title Stronghold ring positions stored per world, 2026-10-27
@@phase worldgen
@@date 2026-10-27
@@jars creativeworldgen
@@prep A: level-type=minecraft:normal generate-structures=true level-seed=8675309
@@text
@@text Creative Common 1.1.03 with `ChunkGeneratorRingCacheMixin` and `worldgen/RingPositionCache` (TODO server #18, perf.md
@@text 11.2 #2). Group A. Fresh world folder; any player with op.
@@text
@@table world
## SQ-RING-01
@group A
@commands Boot a new world; grep latest.log for `[rings]` and `Mixin`; then `/locate structure betterstrongholds:stronghold` (YUNG's replaces the vanilla stronghold) and note the result
@pass One `not stored ... computing` and one `stored in the world's data` line per ring set (vanilla strongholds, Better Strongholds); `<world>/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json` exists with one key per ring set (192 x,z pairs per set in this pack, 2026-10-27 run)
@fails No `[rings]` line: the mixin did not apply (check `m_223148_`; ModernFix `mixin.perf.cache_strongholds=false` must stay in config/modernfix-mixins.properties); `no cache key` warning: read the stack trace (codec encode or probe)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@absent betterstrongholds:stronghold (structure id: listed in kubejs/exported/structures.json worldgen, not in the registry dump)
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): the world folder is the scratch level-name (was world/); the locate names YUNG's stronghold, the
# vanilla one is replaced in this pack (2026-10-27 results), so minecraft:stronghold answered "Could not find"
bootexpect \[rings\] .*not stored for this world and pack, computing
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions stored in the world's data
bootreject \[rings\] .*(could not store|unreadable)
bootreject (?i)Mixin apply failed.*[Rr]ing
shell grep -n "\[rings\]\|Preparing spawn area" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-200
shell L=$(grep -m1 "^level-name=" server.properties | cut -d= -f2); python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); print({k: (len(v) if isinstance(v,list) else type(v).__name__) for k,v in (d.items() if isinstance(d,dict) else [])})" "$L/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json"
> locate structure betterstrongholds:stronghold
waitlog (nearest betterstrongholds:stronghold is at|Could not find a structure of type "?betterstrongholds:stronghold) 300
capture RG nearest betterstrongholds:stronghold is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
look one computing and one stored line per ring set (vanilla, Better Strongholds); the json shape shows one key per set with its pairs; note the stronghold position for SQ-RING-02
## SQ-RING-02
@group A
@commands Locate, `/stop`, boot again (in-row restart); grep `[rings]`; repeat the `/locate`; time "Preparing spawn area" against the first boot
@pass `positions from the world's data` per set, key time well under 1 s; the same locate result; the level-creation stretch about 12 s shorter
@fails `computing` again: the key is not stable between boots (an input is non-deterministic; diff the keys in the file)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@absent betterstrongholds:stronghold (structure id: listed in kubejs/exported/structures.json worldgen, not in the registry dump)
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): the row restarts the server itself (it ran in SQ-RING-01's boot, so the "from the world's data"
# boot never happened) and captures its own first locate before the restart
> locate structure betterstrongholds:stronghold
waitlog (nearest betterstrongholds:stronghold is at|Could not find a structure of type "?betterstrongholds:stronghold) 300
capture RG nearest betterstrongholds:stronghold is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
restart
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions from the world's data
bootreject \[rings\] .*computing
shell grep -n "\[rings\]\|Preparing spawn area" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-200
> locate structure betterstrongholds:stronghold
waitlog nearest betterstrongholds:stronghold is at \[{RG1}, (~|-?\d+), {RG3}\] 300
look the key time well under 1 s; the level-creation stretch about 12 s shorter than the boot before the restart (logs/qrun_bootN.log)
## SQ-RING-03
@group A
@commands Change the seed in `server.properties` and the level-name (a new world), restart; or add a datapack biome change to the same world; boot
@pass `computing` again with a new key; the new positions are stored next to the old entry
@fails Old positions reused: the key misses the changed input
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): the row makes its own new-seed world (edit + restart; it ran in the first boot's world before)
edit sed -i -e 's/^level-seed=.*/level-seed=424242/' -e 's/^level-name=.*/level-name=ring3/' server.properties && grep -q '^level-name=ring3' server.properties
restart
bootexpect \[rings\] .*not stored for this world and pack, computing
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions stored in the world's data
shell L=$(grep -m1 "^level-name=" server.properties | cut -d= -f2); grep -c '"' "$L/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json"; true
look new-seed world (level-name ring3): computing with a new key for each set; a same-world datapack biome change (not done here) would show the old entry beside the new one
@@text
@@text Results 2026-10-27 night: SQ-RING-01 first FAIL: ModernFix's `cache_strongholds` RETURN hook returned before ours, nothing stored (perf.md 12.2 #3); with it off, PASS: 10 `computing` lines (one per dimension with the ring set), 10 `192 positions stored`, file with 10 keys (192 per set in this pack). `/locate structure betterstrongholds:stronghold` (the vanilla stronghold is replaced) -1168 -880 both times. SQ-RING-02 PASS: 10 `from the world's data`, key 8-74 ms, `Done` 5.7 s. SQ-RING-03 PASS: an Overworld biome multiplier change computed a new key for the Overworld only (11 keys), the other 9 read from data; restoring it read the old key again.
